	(lib_symbols)
	(text "BLOCK: nvm_calibration\n\nSCOPE\n  Non-volatile storage for force and temperature calibration and\n  compensation data (REQ-EL-08). I2C1 serial EEPROM per the .ioc\n  (EEPROM_SCL PB8, EEPROM_SDA PB9), with bus pull-ups, write protection\n  and a device-unique ID if the chosen part offers one.\n  Pull-ups follow the even-spacing / paired-alignment rule from\n  /schematic-style - this is the historically missed case.\n\nINTERFACES - the binding contract between blocks.\nReconciled against docs/FAFF-2-Electronics-Full.svg (block diagram) and\nhardware/cubemx/ARIA_SRB_FAFF_2_POC_CBs_1.ioc (MCU pin-map authority).\nNeed something not listed here? Raise it - do not invent it.\n  IN   +3V3, DGND\n  IN/OUT EEPROM_SCL PB8, EEPROM_SDA PB9 (I2C1) <-> mcu\n  IN   nWP control -> mcu (TBC - no .ioc pin allocated yet)\n\nSTATUS: stub. No circuitry drawn yet - this sheet is reserved for the\nfollow-up block task that owns this file. Invoke /schematic-style before\nthe first edit, and delete this note once the block is drawn."
